%
% Backward goal: list membership — the gmeow:listContains backing (#1009 §5).
% Walks the rdf:first/rdf:rest chain (the Prolog analog of the forward-chase
% rl:list-member recursion), reusing the same recursive rdf:List resolution.
% Over the list (x y z) at l0, membership returns Y = {x, y, z}, status ok.
:- prefix(ex, 'https://example.org/profiles/goal-rdf-list-functions/').
:- prefix(rdf, 'http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#').
ex:listMember(L, X) :- rdf:first(L, X).
ex:listMember(L, X) :- rdf:rest(L, R), ex:listMember(R, X).
?- ex:listMember(ex:l0, Y).
